```markdown
---
name: rootless-postgresql
description: Install, initialize, and run a PostgreSQL 17 server and client locally without root privileges on Debian 13 (trixie), for a non-root user (e.g. pete) with a writable /home/project directory. Use when asked to install/start PostgreSQL without sudo, without systemd, or when apt install fails with permission errors.
---

# Rootless PostgreSQL on Debian (user-privilege install)

Installs PostgreSQL server + client as a **non-root user** by downloading Debian
`.deb` packages and extracting them into a user-owned prefix — no `sudo`, no
`apt-get install`, no systemd. Produces a running cluster on a non-default port,
ready to serve a Node/Drizzle (or any) application via `DATABASE_URL`.

Target environment (verified during planning against the user's Debian 13
trixie transcript, 2026-09):

- OS: Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie), `apt-get`/`dpkg-deb` available but **apt
  install requires root** → forbidden for this skill.
- User: unprivileged (e.g. `pete`). `/home/project/` is owned by that user.
- `/usr/lib/locale` contains only `C.utf8` → initdb MUST use `--locale=C.UTF-8`.
- No systemd user session assumed → lifecycle is manual via `pg_ctl`.

## 1. Prerequisites & environment probe

Run these read-only checks first. **Every check must pass before proceeding.**
On failure, print the remediation message and stop — do not guess past a failed
probe.

```bash
set -euo pipefail

# 1. Identity: must be a non-root user with a home directory
[ "$(id -u)" -ne 0 ] || { echo "FAIL: run as non-root user (this skill never uses root)"; exit 1; }

# 2. Target directory writable
mkdir -p /home/project && [ -w /home/project ] \
  || { echo "FAIL: /home/project is not writable by $(id -un)"; exit 1; }

# 3. OS is Debian 13 (trixie) — package names/versions are pinned to trixie
grep -q 'trixie' /etc/os-release \
  || { echo "FAIL: this skill is validated for Debian 13 (trixie) only; adapt version resolution for your release"; exit 1; }

# 4. Required tools present
for t in apt-get apt-cache dpkg-deb ldd curl; do
  command -v "$t" >/dev/null || { echo "FAIL: missing tool: $t"; exit 1; }
done

# 5. Locale: only C.utf8 is guaranteed; initdb will use C.UTF-8
ls /usr/lib/locale | head -3
```

Record the outcomes. If probe 5 shows something other than `C.utf8`, still use
`--locale=C.UTF-8` — it is the only locale guaranteed present on a minimal
Debian image without root-installed locales.

## 2. Configuration (env inputs with sane defaults)

All tunables are environment variables. Defaults match the validated working
setup; override by exporting before running, or by editing the generated
`start_pg.sh` header.

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `PG_MAJOR` | *(auto-resolved, see §3)* | PostgreSQL major version |
| `PG_ROOT` | `/home/project/pgroot` | Extraction prefix for .deb contents |
| `PG_DATA` | `/home/project/pgdata` | Database cluster directory |
| `PG_PORT` | `5435` | **Non-default** port — avoids collision with any system Postgres on 5432 |
| `PG_ROLE` | `fashion_studio_user` | Application role to create |
| `PG_SECRET` | `fashion_studio_secret` | Role password |
| `PG_DB` | `fashion_studio_dev` | Application database |
| `PG_DEB_DIR` | `/home/project/pgdeb` | Staging dir for downloaded .debs |
| `APP_DIR` | `/home/project/moda-fashion-studio` | App whose `.env` gets `DATABASE_URL` |

Secrets default to dev-grade values because this is a local dev cluster bound to
localhost. For anything shared, override `PG_SECRET` and read §9 (hardening).

## 3. Version resolution (dynamic — never hardcode a major)

The failure mode that motivated this skill: `apt-get download postgresql-16`
fails on trixie because trixie ships **17**. Resolve dynamically:

```bash
PG_MAJOR=$(apt-cache search --names-only '^postgresql-[0-9]+$' \
  | grep -oE '[0-9]+' | sort -n | tail -1)
[ -n "$PG_MAJOR" ] || { echo "FAIL: no postgresql-N package found in apt cache"; exit 1; }
echo "Resolved PostgreSQL major: $PG_MAJOR"
```

Do NOT run `apt-get update` — it requires root (lock files under
`/var/lib/apt/lists/`) and will fail with `Permission denied`. The apt cache on
the base image is already populated.

## 4. Download & extract (with iterative dependency resolution)

```bash
mkdir -p "$PG_DEB_DIR" && cd "$PG_DEB_DIR"

# Initial set: server, client, common tooling, client library, perl helpers
PKGS="postgresql-$PG_MAJOR postgresql-client-$PG_MAJOR postgresql-common \
      libpq5 libcommon-sense-perl libjson-perl libtypes-serialiser-perl"

apt-get download $PKGS
```

The hand-picked Perl/lib list above may drift between trixie point releases.
**Verify with `ldd` and iterate** until `postgres` and `psql` have no missing
libraries:

```bash
mkdir -p "$PG_ROOT"
for f in "$PG_DEB_DIR"/*.deb; do dpkg-deb -x "$f" "$PG_ROOT"; done

PGBIN="$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/postgresql/$PG_MAJOR/bin"
PG_LIBDIRS="$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:$PG_ROOT/usr/lib"

missing() {
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PG_LIBDIRS" ldd "$PGBIN/$1" 2>/dev/null \
    | grep 'not found' | awk '{print $1}'
}

# Iterate: download packages that own missing shared objects, re-extract
while true; do
  NEED=""
  for bin in postgres psql initdb pg_ctl; do
    for lib in $(missing "$bin"); do
      owner=$(apt-cache search --names-only . >/dev/null; apt-file search "$lib" 2>/dev/null | head -1 | cut -d: -f1)
      # apt-file may be absent; fallback: query dpkg for the file's package via Contents is unavailable,
      # so fall back to the known trixie naming family:
      [ -n "$owner" ] || owner=$(apt-cache pkgnames | grep -E "^lib${lib%%.*.*}" | head -1)
      NEED="$NEED $owner"
    done
  done
  [ -z "$(echo "$NEED" | tr -d ' ')" ] && break
  echo "Resolving missing libs via: $NEED"
  # shellcheck disable=SC2086
  apt-get download $NEED 2>/dev/null && for f in "$PG_DEB_DIR"/*.deb; do dpkg-deb -x "$f" "$PG_ROOT"; done
done
```

Verification gates for this phase (all must pass):

```bash
[ -x "$PGBIN/initdb" ] || { echo "FAIL: initdb missing after extraction"; exit 1; }
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PG_LIBDIRS" "$PGBIN/initdb" --version   # e.g. initdb (PostgreSQL) 17.11
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PG_LIBDIRS" ldd "$PGBIN/postgres" | grep -q 'not found' \
  && { echo "FAIL: unresolved shared libraries"; exit 1; } || true
```

## 5. Cluster initialization & startup (idempotent `start_pg.sh`)

Generate `/home/project/scripts/start_pg.sh`:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

PG_MAJOR="${PG_MAJOR:?set PG_MAJOR}"; PG_ROOT="${PG_ROOT:-/home/project/pgroot}"
PG_DATA="${PG_DATA:-/home/project/pgdata}"; PG_PORT="${PG_PORT:-5435}"
PG_ROLE="${PG_ROLE:-fashion_studio_user}"; PG_SECRET="${PG_SECRET:-fashion_studio_secret}"
PG_DB="${PG_DB:-fashion_studio_dev}"
PGBIN="$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/postgresql/$PG_MAJOR/bin"
PG_LIBDIRS="$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:$PG_ROOT/usr/lib"
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PG_LIBDIRS${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
export PATH="$PGBIN:$PATH"

mkdir -p "$PG_DATA" /home/project/logs
LOG=/home/project/logs/postgres.log

if [ ! -s "$PG_DATA/PG_VERSION" ]; then
  echo "[pg] initializing cluster at $PG_DATA"
  initdb -D "$PG_DATA" --locale=C.UTF-8 --encoding=UTF8 \
    -U postgres --auth=trust >/dev/null
  # localhost only; non-default port; unix socket inside PG_DATA
  cat >> "$PG_DATA/postgresql.conf" <<EOF
listen_addresses = 'localhost'
port = $PG_PORT
unix_socket_directories = '$PG_DATA'
EOF
fi

if pg_ctl -D "$PG_DATA" status >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  echo "[pg] already running"
else
  echo "[pg] starting postgres on port $PG_PORT"
  pg_ctl -D "$PG_DATA" -l "$LOG" -w start
fi

# Idempotent role/db bootstrap (trust auth on local socket until hardened)
psql -h "$PG_DATA" -U postgres -d postgres -tc \
  "SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname='$PG_ROLE'" | grep -q 1 \
  || psql -h "$PG_DATA" -U postgres -d postgres -c \
     "CREATE ROLE $PG_ROLE LOGIN PASSWORD '$PG_SECRET';"

psql -h "$PG_DATA" -U postgres -d postgres -tc \
  "SELECT 1 FROM pg_database WHERE datname='$PG_DB'" | grep -q 1 \
  || psql -h "$PG_DATA" -U postgres -d postgres -c \
     "CREATE DATABASE $PG_DB OWNER $PG_ROLE;"

echo "[pg] ready: postgresql://$PG_ROLE:$PG_SECRET@localhost:$PG_PORT/$PG_DB"
```

Notes on deliberate choices:

- **Idempotent** — safe to re-run after reboot or crash: skips initdb if
  `PG_VERSION` exists, skips start if already running, guards role/db creation.
- **`--auth=trust` + unix socket in `$PG_DATA`** — trust applies to local
  connections only, and the socket lives in a user-owned dir no other user can
  reach; `listen_addresses='localhost'` prevents remote connections. See §9 for
  the scram upgrade path.
- **`C.UTF-8`** — the only locale guaranteed present without root locales.
- **No edits to `/etc`, no shell rc pollution** — all env is scoped inside the
  script.

## 6. Client wiring for the application

```bash
APP_DIR="${APP_DIR:-/home/project/moda-fashion-studio}"
cd "$APP_DIR"
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env
# Idempotent: replace or append DATABASE_URL
grep -q '^DATABASE_URL=' .env \
  && sed -i "s|^DATABASE_URL=.*|DATABASE_URL=postgresql://$PG_ROLE:$PG_SECRET@localhost:$PG_PORT/$PG_DB|" .env \
  || echo "DATABASE_URL=postgresql://$PG_ROLE:$PG_SECRET@localhost:$PG_PORT/$PG_DB" >> .env
```

Then verify before touching migrations (fail fast, clear cause):

```bash
# TCP readiness + env plumbing
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$PG_LIBDIRS" "$PGBIN/pg_isready" -h localhost -p "$PG_PORT" -d "$PG_DB"
cd "$APP_DIR" && npx tsx -e "import 'dotenv/config'; \
  const u = process.env.DATABASE_URL; \
  if (!u) throw new Error('DATABASE_URL not set'); \
  console.log('DB URL set?', !!u)"
```

Only then:

```bash
cd "$APP_DIR" && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed
```

## 7. Lifecycle commands

```bash
S=/home/project/scripts/start_pg.sh
chmod +x "$S"

# start (idempotent) / stop / status / logs
"$S"
PG_DATA=/home/project/pgdata "$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/postgresql/$PG_MAJOR/bin/pg_ctl" -D /home/project/pgdata stop -m fast
PG_DATA=/home/project/pgdata "$PG_ROOT/usr/lib/postgresql/$PG_MAJOR/bin/pg_ctl" -D /home/project/pgdata status
tail -f /home/project/logs/postgres.log
```

- **No restart persistence** is configured: after a reboot, re-run
  `start_pg.sh`. Do not attempt systemd user units (no dbus/lingering session
  is assumed on the target box) and do not add cron entries unless the user
  explicitly asks.
- Convenience wrapper (optional): `pgctl()` and `psqlr()` shell functions are
  documented in the troubleshooting section rather than installed, to avoid
  mutating the user's rc files.

## 8. Verification ledger (agent must execute & report before claiming done)

| Check | Command (essence) | Pass criterion |
|---|---|---|
| Binaries | `initdb --version` | prints `PostgreSQL <major>` matching resolved version |
| Libraries | `ldd $PGBIN/postgres` | zero `not found` lines |
| Server up | `pg_isready -h localhost -p $PG_PORT` | exit 0, `accepting connections` |
| SQL works | `psql -h $PG_DATA -U postgres -c 'SELECT version();'` | returns version row |
| Role/db exist | query `pg_roles` / `pg_databases` | both present |
| App env | `npx tsx -e "...!!process.env.DATABASE_URL"` | prints `DB URL set? true` |
| App migrations | `npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed` | exit 0 |

Label each result **Verified** (executed & observed), **Reasoned** (inferred
from code), or **Unverifiable** (environment blocked). Never claim "works"
without a ledger entry.

## 9. Hardening (optional, explicit)

Default posture is a localhost-only dev cluster with trust auth on a
user-owned socket. To upgrade before exposing beyond localhost:

```bash
psql -h "$PG_DATA" -U postgres -d postgres \
  -c "ALTER ROLE $PG_ROLE PASSWORD '$PG_SECRET';"   # ensure password set
# in postgresql.conf / pg_hba.conf: scram-sha-256, then reload:
pg_ctl -D "$PG_DATA" reload
```

Do **not** weaken this further (no `listen_addresses = '*'`, no `trust` on TCP)
without stating the tradeoff explicitly.

## 10. Troubleshooting matrix

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `E: Unable to locate package postgresql-16` | Wrong major for trixie | Use §3 dynamic resolution (trixie ships 17) |
| `E: Could not open lock file ... Permission denied` on `apt-get update` | apt needs root | **Never run apt-get update/install**; use `apt-get download` + `dpkg-deb -x` only |
| `error while loading shared libraries: libpq.so.5` | Missing lib after extraction | §4 `ldd` loop; download owning package, re-extract |
| `initdb: invalid locale` | Root-installed locales absent | Always `--locale=C.UTF-8` |
| `port 5435 already in use` | Prior instance or another service | `pg_ctl status`; if foreign service, change `PG_PORT` |
| `FATAL: role "..." does not exist` on re-run | Bootstrap raced or failed | Script is idempotent — re-run `start_pg.sh`; check `postgres.log` |
| `pg_isready: no response` | Server down or wrong port/socket | Start via script; confirm `port` in `postgresql.conf` |
| `DATABASE_URL not set` in app | `.env` not loaded / wrong cwd | Run from `APP_DIR`; verify with the dotenv one-liner in §6 |
| Migrate fails with connection refused | Server not started, or env not saved | Ledger order: server → env → migrate, in that sequence |

## Scope & limitations

- Validated for Debian 13 (trixie); other releases need re-validation of §3/§4.
- Extraction prefix `pgroot` is self-contained; deleting `/home/project/pgroot`
  + `pgdata` fully removes the installation (no system residue by design).
- This skill intentionally performs **no** system-level changes: nothing under
  `/etc`, `/usr` (outside `pgroot`), `/var`, no new users, no sudo.
```


